<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian crude oil, gas output falls in Jan.</title>
<headline>Australian crude oil, gas output falls in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Department of Primary Industries and Energy issued on Friday the following data for Australia's petroleum production in January:</p>
<p>		 Crude Oil  Condensate	Total    Total '000 bpd</p>
<p>			 (megalitres)</p>
<p>Jan 97	   1,858.2	574.1	2,432.2	  493.5</p>
<p>Dec 96 (r)     1,976.5	582.0	2,558.5 (r)    519.1 (r)</p>
<p>Jan 96	   1,897.7	493.3	2,391.0	  485.1</p>
<p>Fiscal 95/96  24,085.2    6,193.3     30,278.4	  521.8</p>
<p>Fiscal 94/95  26,795.0    4,394.5     31,189.6	  537.5</p>
<p>Percentage change on year-to-date:</p>
<p>Fiscal	     5.7	  5.3	   5.7		n/a</p>
<p>Calendar	  -2.1	 16.4	   1.7		n/a</p>
<p>	     Liquefied Petroleum Gas* Ethane	Natural Gas</p>
<p>		   (megalitres)	   (million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Jan 97		281.9		  13.5	   2,225.7</p>
<p>Dec 96		286.9		  13.8	   2,409.5</p>
<p>Jan 96		291.4		  15.8	   2,231.9</p>
<p>Fiscal 95/96    3,649.4		 186.5	  29,984.9</p>
<p>Fiscal 94/95    3,608.8		 203.0	  29,207.6</p>
<p>Percentage change on year-to-date:</p>
<p>Fiscal		 2.8		    -7.5	    -0.5</p>
<p>Calendar	    -3.2		   -14.8	     4.7</p>
<p>NOTE: * Naturally occurring LPG.</p>
<p>One megalitre = 6,290 barrels.</p>
<p>One cubic metre = 35.3 cubic feet</p>
<p>r = revised.  </p>
<p>Fiscal year ends June 30.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
